{"chunk_id": "575dfe547925", "text": "Krishna warns Karna that the world is nearing destruction because Karna refuses to accept the path of righteousness and peace. Karna, resigned to the coming war, tells Krishna that if they survive they will meet again on earth, otherwise in heaven. After Krishna departs unsuccessful in securing peace, Vidura laments to Kunti that Duryodhana\u2019s stubbornness and the influence of men like Karna and Dussasana will inevitably lead to catastrophic war. Kunti, grieving the prospect of kinsmen slaughtering one another, reflects on the terrible choice between war and humiliation. She becomes especially troubled by Karna\u2019s power and hostility toward the Pandavas. Remembering that Karna is secretly her firstborn son, conceived through Surya by a boon from Durvasa, she resolves to reveal the truth and attempt to win him over. She goes to the Ganga and waits as Karna finishes his prayers.\nAfter Krishna fails to secure peace, Vidura laments impending war and Kunti resolves to reveal Karna\u2019s true birth to win him to the Pandavas.\nThemes: inevitability of war, maternal guilt and secrecy, fate and righteousness, loyalty and identity", "vector": [0.011053502559661865, -0.034670840948820114, 0.0021000986453145742, 0.006829915102571249, -0.001006610575132072, 0.028335459530353546, -0.020863987505435944, -0.0026664736215025187, -0.037825167179107666, -0.005322922952473164, 0.01718839630484581, 0.01728195697069168, 0.02193325012922287, 0.022147102281451225, -0.0056069460697472095, -0.004303782247006893, 0.04688716679811478, -0.017549272626638412, 0.034857962280511856, -0.041300270706415176, -0.006716305855661631, -0.0017408932326361537, 0.0033113728277385235, 0.006362112704664469, -0.03090169094502926, 0.025795960798859596, 0.012664079666137695, -0.0300730112940073, 0.015985475853085518, -0.028228534385561943, -0.014421680010855198, 0.009984239935874939, 0.00385268684476614, -0.01745571196079254, -0.0206768661737442, 0.013506123796105